{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And it shall answer for me, etc.</b> If you suspect me of taking anything of yours, it shall answer for me — my righteousness, when my righteousness comes and testifies to my wages before you: that you will find in my flock nothing but speckled and spotted, and whatever you find among them that is not speckled or spotted or brown, it is known that I stole it from you, and it remains in my possession by theft."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:19.867896491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}